// What was happening in the wider world, for the Timeline card's world section
// and the full-screen event view. Dates and facts for the lands of the Bible come
// from the Tyndale Open Bible Dictionary ([[tbd:file:Article]]); for the rest of
// the world from Encyclopaedia Britannica ([[brit:path:Article]]). Never Wikipedia.
// Where the two give different dates, the text says so.
//
// Each event: id, y0/y1 (years, negative is BC), region (for the filters), where
// (the place label), when, title, at ([lat, lng] for the map pin), summary (one
// line), detail (paragraphs, each with its sources) and, optionally:
//   rule     a short name, when the entry is a kingdom, empire or culture that
//            lasted a long time; these make the "Ruling the world then" line
//   touches  [book, first chapter, last chapter] where the Bible names or meets
//            this event; those chapters show it under "Where the world meets the Bible"
//   meets    one sentence, with its source, on how it meets the Bible

const b = (path, title) => `[[brit:${path}:${title}]]`
